{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01TpdtGPYE5wS47ZSyDkmcYf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Implementation complete. `cmd/sponge/main.go` implements all requirements from prd007-sponge:\n\n- **R1**: Core soak-before-write contract with 8192-byte initial buffer, dynamic growth, and temp-file spill when memory threshold is exceeded (RLIMIT_DATA/4 or 256 MB fallback). Temp files created in TMPDIR/tmp with `sponge.` prefix. Signal cleanup handler for SIGINT/SIGTERM/SIGHUP.\n- **R2**: Atomic output via temp-file rename with cross-device copy fallback. Permission preservation via lstat. Default 0666 masked by umask for new files.\n- **R3**: Append mode (`-a`) prepends original file content before stdin content. Non-existent files behave as default mode.\n- **R4**: Passthrough mode writes to stdout when no output file is given, directly from memory for small input or via temp file seek for large input.\n- **R5**: Exit 0 on success, exit 1 with `sponge: <description>` stderr messages on any error. All temp files cleaned up on exit."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":389,"cache_read_input_tokens":86110,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":389},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b76c3fdc-4eec-4396-910f-0ab53d888509","uuid":"949eefb7-8614-4188-aeb8-00734941c1cd"}
